{"id": "EUVD-2015-9430", "enisaUuid": "bf27116f-f63f-3455-bffb-df3b2abdbd70", "description": "Aspose Importer & Exporter plugin for WordPress before 3.0 contains a path traversal vulnerability that allows unauthenticated attackers to download arbitrary files via the unsanitized 'file' parameter. Attackers can send GET requests to aspose_import_export_download.php with traversal sequences like ../../../wp-config.php to read database credentials. Exploitation evidence was first observed by the Shadowserver Foundation on 2023-10-20.", "datePublished": "2026-10-20T20:31:24", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T15:52:13", "baseScore": 8.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://packetstorm.news/files/id/131162/", "https://github.com/projectdiscovery/nuclei-templates/blob/main/http/vulnerabilities/wordpress/aspose-ie-file-download.yaml", "https://wordpress.org/plugins/aspose-importer-exporter/", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/aspose-importer-exporter-wordpress-plugin-3.0-path-traversal-via-aspose-import-export-download-php"], "aliases": ["CVE-2015-20124", "GHSA-4mm5-3w53-cwh2"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.39, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "6264db1e-1354-3517-b81f-958fe344732b", "product": {"name": "Aspose Importer & Exporter", "vendor": {"name": "Aspose"}}, "product_version": "1.0 <3.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "1b5c3616-3836-32fe-987f-f70eed5222b5", "vendor": {"name": "Aspose"}}], "isExploited": false}